Pasal 16

1. Dalam hal tertentu Pemerintah Daerah dapat melakukan kerjasama  dengan:
a. pemerintah daerah lainnya;
b. kepolisian;
c. advokat;
d. tenaga kesehatan;
e. pekerja sosial;
f. relawan pendamping;
g. pembimbing rohani;
h. penegak hukum lainnya, untuk membantu korban dalam proses di  sidang pengadilan;
i. komisi nasional anti kekerasan terhadap perempuan;
j. komisi perlindungan anak Indonesia atau lembaga perlindungan  anak;dan/atau
k. pihak tertentu yang diinginkan demi kepentingan korban.
2. Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa:
a. sosialisasi;
b. pemberian bantuan hukum;
c. pelayanan kesehatan;
d. pendampingan korban;
e. konseling;
f. rehabilitasi sosial;
g. bimbingan rohani; dan/atau
h. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 16

1. In certain circumstances the Regional Government may cooperate with:
a. other regional governments;
b. police;
c. advocates;
d. health workers;
e. social workers;
f. companion volunteers;
g. spiritual counselors;
h. other law enforcers, to assist victims in the court hearing process;
i. national commission on violence against women;
j. Indonesian child protection commission or child protection institutions; and/or
k. certain parties desired for the benefit of victims.
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. socialization;
b. provision of legal aid;
c. health services;
d. victim assistance;
e. counseling;
f. social rehabilitation;
g. spiritual guidance; and/or
h. repatriation and social reintegration.

text:
Pasal 17

1. Bupati melakukan koordinasi perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari  tindak kekerasan dengan:
a. pemerintah;
b. pemerintah provinsi;
c. instansi vertikal;
d. lembaga pendidikan;dane. lembaga kemasyarakatan.
2. Koordinasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:
a. urusan keagamaan;
b. urusan kesehatan;
c. urusan pendidikan;
d. urusan sosial;
e. urusan hukum; dan
f. urusan ketenagakerjaan.

translated_text:
Article 17

1. The Regent coordinates the protection of women and children from acts of violence with:
a. the government;
b. provincial government;
c. vertical agencies;
d. educational institutions; and e. community institutions.
2. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. religious affairs;
b. health affairs;
c. education affairs;
d. social affairs;
e. legal affairs; and
f. manpower affairs.

text:
BAB VII

STANDAR PELAYANAN MINIMAL

Pasal 21

SPM Bidang Layanan Terpadu bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan,  meliputi layanan:
a. penanganan pengaduan/laporan Korban Kekerasan terhadap Perempuan  dan Anak;
b. pelayanan kesehatan bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan;
c. rehabilitasi Sosial bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan;
d. penegakan dan bantuan hukum bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan; dan
e. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VII

MINIMUM SERVICE STANDARDS

Article 21

Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence, include services for:
a. handling complaints/reports of Victims of Violence against Women and Children;
b. health services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
c. Social rehabilitation for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
d. law enforcement and legal aid for Women and Child Victims of Violence; and
e. repatriation and social reintegration for Women and Child Victims of Violence.

text:
Pasal 22

SPM sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 21 memiliki indikator kinerja meliputi:
a. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan yang mendapatkan  penanganan pengaduan oleh petugas terlatih di dalam unit pelayanan  terpadu;
b. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan yang mendapatkan  layanan kesehatan oleh tenaga kesehatan terlatih di Puskesmas dan di  Rumah Sakit;
c. cakupan layanan Rehabilitasi Sosial yang diberikan oleh petugas  Rehabilitasi Sosial terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan  di dalam unit pelayanan terpadu;
d. cakupan layanan bimbingan rohani yang diberikan oleh petugas  bimbingan rohani terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan di  dalam unit pelayanan terpadu;
e. cakupan penegakan hukum dari tingkat penyidikan sampai dengan  putusan pengadilan atas kasus-kasus Kekerasan terhadap Perempuan  dan Anak;
f. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan yang mendapatkan  layanan bantuan hukum;
g. cakupan layanan Pemulangan bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan; dan
h. cakupan layanan reintegrasi sosial bagi Perempuan dan Anak Korban  Kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 22

Minimum Service Standards as referred to in Article 21 have performance indicators including:
a. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated service units;
b. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Community Health Centers and Hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of Violence against Women and Children;
f. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women and Child Victims of Violence; and
h. coverage of social reintegration services for Women and Child Victims of Violence.
